Hoo boy.  More adventures with my tournament valkyrie.  I went down to
Minetown without my pet arch-lich so he wouldn't kill everyone.  I
NEVER wanted an arch-lich for a pet and I planned to leave him at the
bottom of the mines.  Well, I stayed a little too long shop-IDing and
when I returned to the level above Minetown Fyodor the arch-lich had
become peaceful.  But that's not the problem.  Well that's okay, I
thought, probably not the best place to have a lich wandering around
but it could be worse.  Carried on playing with my other pet, Ivan the
grey dragon.  Everything went great.  Sokoban had a BoH and I picked up
a bunch of great armour just sitting around the dungeon, most notably a
blessed +4 pair of iron shoes.  And then all the weapons, wands and
intrinsics that I'd been missing throughout the early game started
coming in.  That MMF at the bottom of the Mines?  It turned out not to
be the bottom after all - I just turned and ran before I got a good
look.  But anyway, I killed it and all was well.  It wasn't a bones
level either, and the MMF wasn't from a polymorph trap so I guess the
RNG was just having a little fun.  Anyway I'm saying all this because
this is pretty much my YASD thread.

Because, see, somewhere, somehow, I got see invisible.  Now that I
think about it it must have been from that potion of "fruit juice" I
drank down in Minetown.  But anyway, on the level above Minetown, I saw
Fyodor turn himself invisible.  But that was cool.  I could still see
him.  I assumed I'd always be able to see him.

*sigh*

Soooo I gathered all my junk and went back up to level 2, had a little
swim with some useless potions and made a stack of holy water, then
proceeded to have a little bless-fest.  I blessed my 3 ?oID and the
first one identified everything.  I noticed I had enough money for more
protection.  I go back down to Minetown...

And then suddenly on the level above I meet my lich again, except this
time I can't see him.  Thanks to server lag, I walk right into him
several times.  Yeah, I know, you have to watch where you walk with
lag, especially on a level with an INVISIBLE ARCH-LICH on it.  Aaargh.
So my messages went something like "Wait, there's something there you
can't see!  You anger it!  You idiot!  It clears its throat.  It takes
off half your health!  Do you have any last wishes?"

And the *really* ironic thing is, I had a ?oGenocide and some holy
water and was mulling over whether to genocide L or R but decided to
wait because I was low on holy water.  But it's too late now because
both items are in my bag next to my many wands of digging and scrolls
of teleport (Yes, I know I'm supposed to keep some in my main inventory
but I forget a lot.  I don't think I'll be forgetting after this.) and
I don't think I'll have time to get them out.  Meanwhile, Ivan the
unhelpful dragon is off eating gnomes.  My pets are all ungrateful
meatbags, I tell you.

I don't think I'll be playing any more today.  If I don't think of any
wonderful escape tricks by tomorrow I'll just try getting out the ol'
wand o' digging and see if it works.  But I'm pretty sure I'm doomed.
Remember, kids: don't leave invisible arch-lichs wandering around the
dungeon!


